{"name":"Drunken Dragonfly","hex":"#33dd88","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"drunken","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["past participle of drink"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Drunk, in the state of intoxication after having drunk an alcoholic beverage.","Given to habitual excessive use of alcohol."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drunken"},{"term":"dragonfly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An insect of the suborder Epiprocta or, more strictly, the infraorder Anisoptera, having four long transparent wings held perpendicular to a long body when perched."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dragonfly"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alcohol intoxication","blocks":[{"text":"Alcohol intoxication, commonly described in higher doses as drunkenness or inebriation, and known in overdose as alcohol poisoning, is the behavior and physical effects caused by recent consumption of alcohol. The technical term intoxication in common speech may suggest that a large amount of alcohol has been consumed, leading to accompanying physical symptoms and deleterious health effects. Mild intoxication is mostly referred to by slang terms such as tipsy or buzzed. In addition to the toxicity of ethanol, the main psychoactive component of alcoholic beverages, other physiological symptoms may arise from the activity of acetaldehyde, a metabolite of alcohol. These effects may not arise until hours after ingestion and may contribute to a condition colloquially known as a hangover."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Michelangelo_drunken_Noah.jpg/330px-Michelangelo_drunken_Noah.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcohol_intoxication"},{"title":"Dragonfly","blocks":[{"text":"A dragonfly is a flying insect belonging to the suborder Anisoptera of the order Odonata. About 3,000 living species of dragonflies are known. Most are tropical, with fewer species in temperate regions. Loss of wetland habitat threatens dragonfly populations around the world. Adult dragonflies are characterised by a pair of large, multifaceted, compound eyes, two pairs of strong, transparent wings, sometimes with coloured patches, and an elongated body. Many dragonflies have brilliant iridescent or metallic colours produced by structural coloration, making them conspicuous in flight. An adult dragonfly's compound eyes have nearly 24,000 ommatidia each."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Red_grasshawk_%28Neurothemis_fluctuans%29_male_Phuket_2.jpg/330px-Red_grasshawk_%28Neurothemis_fluctuans%29_male_Phuket_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragonfly"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/The_wine_is_a_mocker_1663-1664_Jan_Steen.jpg/500px-The_wine_is_a_mocker_1663-1664_Jan_Steen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/The_wine_is_a_mocker_1663-1664_Jan_Steen.jpg/1280px-The_wine_is_a_mocker_1663-1664_Jan_Steen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/The_wine_is_a_mocker_1663-1664_Jan_Steen.jpg/500px-The_wine_is_a_mocker_1663-1664_Jan_Steen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wine is a Mocker by Jan Steen c. 1663","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_wine_is_a_mocker_1663-1664_Jan_Steen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/%28Five_stages_of_inebriation%2C_ca.1863-1868%29_-_photographer_Charles_Percy_Pickering_%289610229733%29_%282%29.jpg/500px-%28Five_stages_of_inebriation%2C_ca.1863-1868%29_-_photographer_Charles_Percy_Pickering_%289610229733%29_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=e